From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winex11, explorer: a Linux program's window in a Wine window

Every Wine window lives in Wine's desktop, one X window; a Linux program's
window (Xwayland, the same X server) was a top-level of its own beside it,
so it was above every Wine window or below them all -- never between (David
2026-10-01/02: Linux windows "should stack like regular Windows windows").

The taskbar's window for each Linux window (explorer's SgLinuxWindow, from
the compositor's list) is now a real Wine window around it: winex11
reparents the program's window into its client area (sg_embed.c, asked with
WM_X11DRV_SG_EMBED_QUERY/ATTACH), as a window manager frames a client -- in
the save-set, so it outlives the shell; sized to the client area and the
frame to it; its title followed; closed with WM_DELETE_WINDOW. It is then a
Wine window to the whole shell: stacked among the others, activated,
minimized (to its button) and snapped, in Alt+Tab, Task View and Task
Manager. The X focus goes to the program when its frame is activated; a
click into the program activates the frame first (a synchronous button grab
on the frame, the press replayed); the Windows key, Alt+Tab, Alt+F4 and
Ctrl+Shift+Esc are grabbed on the frame, the shell's still. Wine's window
surface paints around it (ClipByChildren), and X errors on it (it may go
at any moment) are expected. A window that cannot be framed keeps the
hidden stand-in, tried again a few times.

sg-compositor (sg24) stops listening to a window Wine reparented: wlroots'
window manager undid every focus change into it.

Gate: test/linuxembed-gate.sh (mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_EMBED,
SG_MUTANT_EMBED_NO_FOCUS, SG_MUTANT_EMBED_NO_CLICK_FOCUS,
SG_MUTANT_EMBED_PAINT_OVER fail it).
